# Open House, flown from the Furnace Room to the star in the Belfry.
#
# This is the acceptance run for docs/PLAN.md Stage 2's "completable headlessly by a
# scripted run". It starts where the house starts -- no `room` or `where` line, so the
# glider appears at the house's own `initial 32 112` in room 4 -- and it finishes by
# collecting the only star, which sets gameOver. See TestOpenHouseCanBeFinished.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What the keystrokes are doing, and why there are so many
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The house is 43 rooms; this route touches ten of them, climbing six staircases:
#
#   4 Furnace Room (f1 s57) -up-> 10 Front Hall -east-> 11 Parlour -up->
#   21 Nursery -east-> 22 Sewing Room -up-> 30 Attic Stair -east->
#   31 Cedar Closet -up-> 36 Tower Landing -east-> 37 Tower Stair -up-> 41 Belfry
#
# Every `-` is a released right-arrow and every `right` is it pressed again, and the
# alternation is not fiddliness -- it is the game. A glider crossing a vent's 52 px
# catchment at cruise (5 px/frame) is inside it for about ten frames and rises 6 px on
# each, so it gains **60 px** of height and spends 0.6 px of height on every px it
# travels. Break-even is a vent every 100 px. Two vents in a 512 px room is nowhere
# near that, so holding the arrow down loses roughly 100 px of altitude per room and
# kills the glider in three: the trace of that run reaches room 12 at top 222 and dies
# in room 13.
#
# So the glider has to stop in each column and let it carry it to the ceiling before
# going on, and that -- not the layout -- is what the house teaches. It is also why the
# originals average only 1.49 blowers per room (docs/analysis/original-houses.md 10.2)
# and are no more crossable at a constant hold than this one is: riding the updraft is
# the mechanic, and a house that could be flown with the key held down would have
# removed it.
#
# The other thing the alternation does is take the staircases. MoveItUp fires on
# GliderInRect(112x32 at (H,28)) **and** !HeldRight, so the glider passes a staircase it
# is flying at and climbs one it stops at. In this route the arrow is released inside the
# trigger box -- h 336..400, v 28..40 -- at f=87, 325, 564, 803 and 1042, and every one
# of those is a deliberate release rather than a coincidence of timing.
#
# The last release, f=1087, is the star: the glider is over the gap between the Belfry's
# two vents, and letting go drops it straight through the kStar at h 240..272, v 262..293.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Regenerating it
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The frame numbers came out of the physics rather than out of arithmetic on paper,
# because the 60 px figure above is a property of the simulation and not of the file. If
# a change to the flight model moves them, the way to find the new ones is the rule set
# this route follows, which is short enough to state: hold right; release on the first
# frame the glider rises above 24; press right again when it reaches top 14; and in a
# staircase room, release instead on the first frame inside the trigger box. Applying
# those four rules frame by frame reproduces every number below.
#
# A failure here is a flight-model change, and the room the trace stops in says which
# leg stopped working. It is not a house bug unless the house changed.

house Open House
seed 1
frames 1200
neighbors 9
players 1
sound off
clock 1994-10-14T10:09:00Z

# room 4, The Furnace Room -- lifted off the h 120 vent, across to the h 300 one,
# then released in the staircase's box at f=87.
at 0 right
at 17 -
at 23 right
at 58 -
at 74 right
at 87 -

# room 10, The Front Hall -- arrives from the stairs at left 127 top 52, which is
# inside the h 120 catchment, so the vent takes it. Then east to h 336 and out.
at 112 right
at 152 -
at 172 right

# room 11, The Parlour -- entered from the west at top 114; h 120, then h 300, then
# the box.
at 231 -
at 259 right
at 295 -
at 312 right
at 325 -

# room 21, The Nursery, and east into room 22
at 351 right
at 391 -
at 411 right

# room 22, The Sewing Room
at 470 -
at 498 right
at 534 -
at 551 right
at 564 -

# room 30, The Attic Stair, and east into room 31
at 590 right
at 630 -
at 650 right

# room 31, The Cedar Closet
at 709 -
at 737 right
at 773 -
at 790 right
at 803 -

# room 36, The Tower Landing, and east into room 37
at 829 right
at 869 -
at 889 right

# room 37, The Tower Stair
at 948 -
at 976 right
at 1012 -
at 1029 right
at 1042 -

# room 41, The Belfry -- up off the h 120 vent, east over the gap, and let go.
at 1068 right
at 1087 -
